{"packet_id":"D043-01","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"No-fault eviction relocation assistance and LAHD Declaration of Intent filing","requirement":"Before evicting a tenant for a no-fault reason, the landlord must pay relocation assistance and file a Declaration of Intent to Evict with LAHD; a copy of the termination notice must be filed within 3 days of service.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Tenants in rental units covered by the Rent Stabilization Ordinance (RSO) or the Just Cause Ordinance (JCO) in the City of Los Angeles.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Units covered by the RSO or JCO"},"exemptions":"No relocation assistance is owed when replacing a resident manager, or when an eviction is required by hazardous conditions caused by a natural disaster not caused by the landlord's negligence; a landlord may offset unpaid rent.","penalty":"Failure to file the Landlord Declaration makes the eviction a violation of the RSO or JCO; a tenant may raise non-payment of relocation assistance as an affirmative defense.","effective_date":null,"citation":"L.A. Mun. Code § 151.09","quoted_span":"All tenant not- at-fault evictions require payment of relocation assistance and the filing of a Declaration of Intent to Evict form with the Los Angeles Housing Department (LAHD) before evicting tenants from units covered by the Rent Stabilization Ordinance (RSO) or the Just Cause Ordinance (JCO).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-01","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"RSO/JCO not-at-fault eviction grounds","requirement":"A landlord may recover possession without tenant fault only for the listed reasons, which include owner or relative occupancy, resident manager occupancy, demolition or removal from rental housing, an order to vacate, HUD sale, hotel conversion and conversion to affordable housing.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental units covered by the RSO or JCO; the condominium, cooperative, community apartment, hotel and commercial conversion ground applies regardless of RSO or JCO coverage.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Units covered by the RSO or JCO"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"L.A. Mun. Code § 165.03","quoted_span":"The landlord evicts for the occupancy of her/himself, spouse, grandchildren, children, parents or grandparents, or a resident manager (Los Angeles Municipal Code (LAMC) 151.09.A.8, 165.03.H.).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-01","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"RSO/JCO relocation assistance amounts, July 2026 through June 2027","requirement":"A landlord displacing a tenant for a no-fault reason must pay the charted relocation amount, which depends on whether the tenant is eligible or qualified and on the length of tenancy, with the amounts set for July 1, 2026 through June 30, 2027.","key_value":"Eligible: $11,000 (under 3 years) / $14,400 (3 or more years or low income); Qualified: $23,150 / $27,400; eff. 7/1/2026-6/30/2027","coverage_conditions":"Tenants displaced for a no-fault eviction under the RSO or JCO; relocation assistance is paid per unit, not per tenant.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Tenants displaced for a no-fault eviction under the RSO or JCO"},"exemptions":"The amounts do not apply where the eviction is demolition of a Protected Unit for new construction and the tenant is lower income (80% AMI or lower).","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2026-07-01","citation":"L.A. Mun. Code § 165.06","quoted_span":"Chart A: Relocation Assistance Amounts\nEffective July 1, 2026 through June 30, 2027","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-01","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Relocation assistance payment deadline of 15 days","requirement":"The landlord must make relocation assistance available within 15 days of serving the written notice of eviction; if escrow is used, the money must be deposited within that period and paid within three working days of a request.","key_value":"15 days","coverage_conditions":"Relocation assistance payments owed to tenants displaced for a no-fault eviction under the RSO or JCO.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Relocation payments under the RSO or JCO"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"RAC Regulations § 960.00","quoted_span":"Payment shall be made available within fifteen (15) days of service of the written notice of eviction","interaction":null,"confidence":0.7,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-01","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Reduced relocation assistance for Mom and Pop properties and single-family dwellings","requirement":"Mom and Pop properties may pay reduced relocation assistance for good faith owner or eligible-relative occupancy evictions; a single-family dwelling owned by a natural person who owns no more than four units gets one month's rent as payment or credit.","key_value":"Reduced relocation assistance; one month's rent (single-family dwellings)","coverage_conditions":"Evictions for owner, eligible relative or resident manager occupancy; the reduced fee requires a building with four or fewer rental units and no use of the provision in the previous three years.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":4,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Owner, eligible relative or resident manager occupancy evictions"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"L.A. Mun. Code § 151.30","quoted_span":"Mom and Pop properties may pay reduced relocation assistance payments to their tenants for a good faith eviction for occupancy by the owner or eligible relative, provided that requirements in Section 151.30 of the LAMC are met.  This applies only for evictions for occupancy by owner, family, or manager.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D043-01","doc_id":"D043","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Resident Protections Ordinance relocation duties and penalties","requirement":"An owner demolishing a Protected Unit for new construction within five years of filing notice must comply with RPO relocation requirements, including rights to relocation, six-month notice, return and first refusal; violations face penalties starting at $250,000 per displaced unit.","key_value":"$250,000 per displaced unit minimum penalty","coverage_conditions":"Protected Units demolished for new construction; all displaced tenants receive at least RSO or JCO amounts, enhanced for lower income households under the HCA or RPO.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Protected Units demolished for new construction"},"exemptions":"The regular RSO or JCO relocation rules apply if the units demolished are not Protected Units or are not occupied by a lower income tenant.","penalty":"Financial penalties starting at $250,000 per displaced unit and withholding of LAHD permit clearances.","effective_date":"2025-02-11","citation":"Ordinances 188481 & 188482 (Los Angeles Resident Protections Ordinance)","quoted_span":"Owners who demolish a Protected Unit for the purpose of new construction within 5 years after the filing of the Notice of Intent to Withdraw or Declaration of Intent to Evict with LAHD are required to comply with relocation requirements under the RPO. Failure to comply with the RPO may result in financial penalties starting at $250,000 per displaced unit and withholding of LAHD permit clearances.","interaction":"Owner must pay the higher of State Housing Crisis Act or City RSO/JCO/RPO relocation amounts.","confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
